{"v":1,"duration":137.322,"text":"Hi, my name is Bunlong Heng. I am a Senior Full-Stack Developer with over 12 years of experience building web applications and owning them end to end. I graduated from UMass Lowell with a degree in Computer Science in 2014, and throughout my career I have worked across the entire stack, from React and Node J S to A P I's, databases, cloud, security, and performance. Most recently, I have been working at Thrive. One project I am especially proud of is the Advanced Campaign Editor for the Thrive Business Center. I helped lead and build it using React and Node J S, with backend A P I's and Amazon S three. I also worked heavily on the Reporting Center, including the Keep and Thrive integration, where I helped plan how reporting data should flow between the systems securely and accurately. Performance was a big focus for me there. One of my favorite wins was bringing our dashboard response time down from around five seconds to under half a second. I also worked on observability, security and performance readiness, and mentoring developers. I am A W S certified as both a Solutions Architect Associate and Developer Associate. Lately, though, I have gotten really into auditing. I audit repositories, P R's, Jira epics, and even projects that span multiple repositories. The project I am most excited about is something I built called Repo Audit. Repo Audit reverse-engineers a codebase across ten different engineering lenses, including architecture, security, performance, testing, maintainability, and code quality, and brings everything together into one structured report. I have run more than 500 audits with it so far. But the main reason I built it is actually pretty simple: I want to become a better developer. It lets me go back through my own work, find mistakes, learn from decisions I have made in the past, and bring those lessons into whatever I build next. It also acts as a quality gate. Before I release or open-source something, I can audit it and make sure the code I am putting my name on meets my standards. And as A I gets better, the audits get better too. I can revisit older projects and keep learning from them. That is really how I approach engineering. I love building, I love staying hands-on, and I am always looking for ways to build better software and become a better developer. Thanks for taking the time to learn a little bit about me.","starts":[0,0.186,0.302,0.325,0.36,0.406,0.441,0.499,0.522,0.569,0.604,0.639,0.673,0.708,0.743,0.801,0.836,0.894,0.94,1.01,1.068,1.091,1.115,1.173,1.207,1.289,1.335,1.405,1.463,1.521,1.579,1.66,1.707,1.753,1.8,1.823,1.869,1.904,1.962,1.997,2.043,2.078,2.101,2.148,2.183,2.241,2.264,2.287,2.322,2.345,2.38,2.438,2.473,2.496,2.566,2.589,2.647,2.682,2.728,2.786,2.844,2.902,2.961,2.995,3.065,3.111,3.146,3.181,3.204,3.251,3.297,3.344,3.39,3.425,3.483,3.692,3.773,3.796,3.82,3.855,3.889,3.924,3.971,4.005,4.04,4.063,4.122,4.168,4.238,4.319,4.365,4.412,4.447,4.481,4.516,4.551,4.598,4.632,4.667,4.702,4.737,4.772,4.818,4.865,4.888,4.911,4.957,4.992,5.062,5.108,5.166,5.201,5.248,5.283,5.329,5.375,5.445,5.538,5.596,5.642,5.677,5.724,5.77,5.817,5.851,5.886,5.921,6.014,6.084,6.13,6.177,6.223,6.246,6.281,6.339,6.362,6.385,6.455,6.502,6.594,6.664,6.699,6.734,6.769,6.803,6.838,6.919,6.989,7.035,7.128,7.221,7.465,7.523,7.639,7.674,7.732,7.778,7.848,7.906,7.976,8.034,8.092,8.127,8.161,8.196,8.231,8.266,8.289,8.37,8.452,8.521,8.603,8.626,8.649,8.719,8.765,8.835,8.881,8.939,8.986,9.032,9.102,9.125,9.16,9.195,9.218,9.253,9.276,9.334,9.369,9.427,9.473,9.52,9.578,9.636,9.682,9.705,9.74,9.798,9.833,9.88,9.926,9.984,10.042,10.1,10.147,10.17,10.216,10.251,10.309,10.402,10.472,10.507,10.541,10.576,10.611,10.646,10.681,10.739,10.913,11.157,11.482,11.76,11.819,11.865,11.923,11.969,12.004,12.039,12.062,12.097,12.12,12.144,12.178,12.213,12.248,12.271,12.306,12.341,12.387,12.422,12.469,12.538,12.573,12.643,12.689,12.759,12.817,12.852,12.933,12.956,13.026,13.049,13.096,13.13,13.165,13.212,13.